WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
The project was struggling, which was I talk about these as 2 different ways of

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Concealing the bad news that's going on in a project, and stopping those things from getting fixed. One is a kind of baby seal, and the other one is a big bad dog, and ironically, the baby seal is the more dangerous one of these two

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:32.000
So basically what this was, and I've seen this on several projects, is that as you start to improve, as you start to do the iterative

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:50.000
As you start to do the iterative things to kind of increase the odds of the project succeeding, you will encounter things that need fixing. You will encounter problems, you will encounter difficulties. And in order to get these fixed, very often you have to escalate them

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:02.000
And by doing that, by starting to escalate these things, you start to carve out what the real what the real kind of shape of the project is and what the real risks are and what the real challenges are.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:19.000
And if there's real risks and challenges are quite scary, one of the things that senior management can do is to try and stop hearing about them. And one of the ways they can do that is to just put the mildest mannered, nicest person possible

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:29.000
In charge of reporting directly to whoever is the people in the senior hierarchy.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.000
